# Skills installed into the canonical pool at ~/.agents/skills.
#
# Every harness except Claude Code reads that path natively; `npx skills` writes the
# one adapter symlink Claude Code needs. Format: <owner/repo> <skill>
#
# Add a line, run `agent-setup`. Remove a line and the skill stays on disk until you
# run `npx skills remove <skill>` - deliberately, so nothing disappears silently.

vercel-labs/agent-browser        agent-browser
addyosmani/agent-skills          documentation-and-adrs
mattpocock/skills                grilling
mattpocock/skills                improve-codebase-architecture
kunchenguid/lavish-axi           lavish
daymade/claude-code-skills       ui-designer

# --- deliberately NOT installed -------------------------------------------------
#
# Superseded generations. Pocock renamed these; you had three layers installed at
# once and none was current. If you want that flow back, install to-spec / to-tickets
# rather than any of these:
#   mattpocock/skills   grill-me            -> superseded by grilling
#   mattpocock/skills   grill-with-docs     -> superseded by grilling
#   mattpocock/skills   write-a-prd         -> superseded by to-spec
#   mattpocock/skills   prd-to-issues       -> superseded by to-tickets
#
# Duplicates of something already present:
#   anthropics/skills   frontend-design     -> the frontend-design plugin covers this
#
# Kept despite overlap with superpowers (superpowers is not installed, so this is
# the TDD skill the implementer agent references):
#   mattpocock/skills   tdd
#
# Works against a curated setup by design:
#   vercel-labs/skills  find-skills         -> exists to install more skills globally
#
# In the pool from earlier experiments, never linked into a harness:
#   fastapi, fastapi-expert, pytest, python-async-patterns,
#   python-patterns, python-testing-patterns
